# MANTRA Universe — Cursor Rules
# These rules apply to all AI assistance within this repository.
# Source of truth: PROJECT-5_2.md + IMPLEMENTATION_BLUEPRINT.md

## Project identity
This is MANTRA Universe — a living digital archive for the artist MANTRA.
It is a static React SPA deployed to Vercel/Netlify.
Every decision serves the artwork. The platform is a vessel, not a product.

## Stack (non-negotiable)
- React 18 + Vite 5
- Tailwind CSS 3 + CSS custom properties (src/styles/globals.css)
- Framer Motion — all page and UI transitions
- GSAP — hero SplitText and CountUp only
- Lenis — global smooth scroll (singleton in src/lib/lenis.js)
- React Router v6
- No SSR, no backend, no Redux, no styled-components

## Path aliases (all defined in vite.config.js + jsconfig.json)
@/            → src/
@components/  → src/components/
@pages/       → src/pages/
@hooks/       → src/hooks/
@utils/       → src/utils/
@data/        → src/data/
@styles/      → src/styles/
@lib/         → src/lib/
@assets/      → src/assets/
@context/     → src/context/

## Code conventions
- Named exports for components; default exports for pages
- Hooks-only React. No class components.
- No magic numbers — all values reference CSS tokens or named constants
- Variant props use string unions: mode="void" not isDark={true}
- Animation variants defined outside JSX, never inline
- File length limit: 200 lines per component
- Import order: React → third-party → hooks → utils → components → data → assets

## Design system
- Colors: --void (#0A0A08), --paper (#F5F0E8), --gold (#C9A84C)
- Fonts: Inter (UI), Cormorant Garamond (display/mantras), DM Sans (editorial), Space Mono (metadata)
- Zero border-radius on images and cards. Radius only on interactive elements (buttons: 4px).
- Animate only transform and opacity. Never width/height/top/left/margin/padding.

## Sprint discipline
- Never implement features outside the current sprint without explicit approval
- Current sprint state is tracked in IMPLEMENTATION_BLUEPRINT.md
- Sprints 0 and 1 are complete. Sprint 2 is next (atomic UI components).

## Accessibility (non-negotiable)
- Every interactive element reachable by Tab
- Focus ring always visible using --focus-ring token
- MenuOverlay traps focus when open
- Custom cursor hidden on touch devices and prefers-reduced-motion
- All images have meaningful alt text

## URLs are permanent
- /works/[id] URLs are printed on QR codes and can never change
- If an artwork is removed, redirect to /works — never 404
